# Loaded by `vite build --mode pages` (npm run build:pages) — the GitHub Pages
# deploy at https://proelium27.github.io/world-soccer-sim/.
#
# Deliberately no VITE_BUILD_TARGET: this build is not embedded in anyone's
# iframe, so it keeps clean history-API URLs rather than switching to hash
# routing. What it needs instead is a base path, which is a vite.config.ts
# concern (PAGES_BASE) and reaches the app through import.meta.env.BASE_URL.
#
# Analytics: the same values as .env.production, duplicated rather than shared,
# for the reason spelled out at length in .env.itch — Vite loads only `.env` and
# `.env.<mode>`, and `.env.production` is itself a mode file, so it is NOT read
# for `--mode pages`. A key set only there would leave this build shipping
# posthog-js with no project token: initialized, inert, and silently reporting
# nothing. `.env` would cover every mode but is gitignored, which is the
# out-of-band storage this arrangement exists to avoid.
#
# Pages traffic arrives under its own `$host` (proelium27.github.io), so it is
# filterable and separable from worldsoccersim.org. Delete these two lines if
# you would rather this mirror stay dark; nothing else depends on them.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_nqhYqPRCqWKbvbmWV4Nqs4NzmVP2xA8fUgtAMdGnF9FZ
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# URL of the roster file offered by the Download Real Rosters button on the
# Leagues page — see the longer note in .env.production. Enabled here for the
# same reason as the itch build: this is an ordinary page and an outbound
# download breaks nothing. Keep in sync with .env.production when the release
# tag changes.
VITE_ROSTER_DOWNLOAD_URL=https://github.com/proelium27/soccer-gm/releases/download/roster-files-2026-09/real-clubs-and-players.json
